    {
      "keys": "⌥ (left)",
      "keys_raw": "left_alt",
      "action": "Make left Option a lazy modifier",
      "description": "Remaps left_option to itself with lazy:true, so the Option key_down is not posted until another key is pressed with it",
      "category": "misc",
      "mode": "global",
      "origin": "custom",
      "source": "home/dot_config/private_karabiner/karabiner.json:596",
      "notes": "Not a hotkey. The enclosing rule is described as 'no special characters', but per the Karabiner docs `lazy` only defers the modifier's own key event — it does NOT stop macOS from composing ø/∂/˙ from Option+letter. What actually makes Alt+arrow reach Zellij/Neovim is Ghostty's `macos-option-as-alt = true` plus the option+left/right unbinds (home/dot_config/ghostty/config:5,11-12). Effect of this rule is limited to suppressing bare-Option key events.",
